{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-05T13:53:38.768Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. All acceptance criteria are met and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the validator's archive-time observation run:\n\n**`src/watcher/validator.ts`** (new, 249 lines) — `runValidator` orchestrates the run: disabled/missing validator returns early; otherwise it selects the `Vcs`, reads inputs via `readValidatorInputs`, records `not_run` with a reason when needed, writes `diff.patch`/`scenarios.md` (removing old findings), snapshots+restores the tree, spawns the adapter once (passed one or `getHarnessAdapter`), resolves the outcome (`timed_out`/`failed`/`unreadable`/`validated`), appends one `validator_ran` event, and always removes `.run/validator/`. Every error is caught with `validator failed: <message>` logging and a best-effort `failed` event.\n\n**`src/watcher/validator-guard.ts`** (new) — `snapshotValidatorTree`/`restoreValidatorTree` record `vcs.status()` and file bytes before the spawn, then put back changed paths (restore bytes, remove if absent before, or `vcs.discard`), returning sorted project-relative restored paths.\n\n**`src/watcher/archiver.ts`** — `checkAndArchiveSpec` gained the optional `CheckAndArchiveOptions` fourth argument and calls `runValidator` after the check passes and before relocation. File is 215 lines; the function is 78 lines.\n\n**`tests/validator-run.test.ts`** (new) — 7 tests covering every archive-run and tree-guard scenario with a fake adapter, in a linked `osq/001-validator` worktree and outside git for the `not_run` cases.\n\nVerification: task verify green (7/7), line/function budgets, no-`skipped` check, and the full `pnpm verify` (typecheck, UI build, all tests, lint) all pass. Result written to `openspec/changes/149-validator-observe/.run/results/5.md`."}}
